messages:
eli: Getting a bunch of tickets from new users hitting import issues with the JS SDK. Quickstart uses one style and it fails in several environments.
nora: Which combos are failing?
eli: Node CJS (no "type":"module"), Node ESM, TypeScript without esModuleInterop, and edge runtimes like Vercel/Cloudflare.
kevin: Typical errors: "named export not found" when people do `import { InferenceClient } from '@redwood/inference'` but package is shipped with a default-only export; or `undefined` after `require()` when the consumer expects named fields.
eli: Can we ship a short cheatsheet in the SDK README and add 4 tiny example apps? People just want copy/paste that works.
kevin: Agreed. Proposed README snippets to cover the common cases:
```
// CommonJS (package.json without "type": "module")
const Redwood = require('@redwood/inference');
const client = new Redwood.InferenceClient({ apiKey: process.env.RW_KEY });

// ESM default import ("type": "module")
import Redwood from '@redwood/inference';
const client = new Redwood.InferenceClient({ apiKey: process.env.RW_KEY });

// ESM named import (preferred in ESM-only runtimes)
import { InferenceClient } from '@redwood/inference';
const client2 = new InferenceClient({ apiKey: process.env.RW_KEY });

// TypeScript (if you can't enable esModuleInterop)
import Redwood = require('@redwood/inference');
const clientTs = new (Redwood as any).InferenceClient({ apiKey: process.env.RW_KEY });
```
nora: Also include a tiny tsconfig snippet to reduce friction for TS newcomers:
```json
{
  "compilerOptions": {
    "esModuleInterop": true,
    "allowSyntheticDefaultImports": true
  }
}
```
eli: For edge runtimes, call out explicitly: they only support ESM. Show an Edge example (Vercel/Cloudflare) with named import.
kevin: Example for Edge (short):
```
import { InferenceClient } from '@redwood/inference';
export default async function handler(req) {
  const c = new InferenceClient({ apiKey: process.env.RW_KEY });
  const out = await c.generate({ prompt: 'hello' });
  return new Response(JSON.stringify(out));
}
```
dev-tools-bot: Created draft docs PR: https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/520 - adds "JS SDK: CJS / ESM / TS / Edge" section and links to examples.
kevin: Operational notes for eng-build: ensure package.json exposes both `main` (CJS) and `module` (ESM), types point at .d.ts, and CI publishes both dist/cjs and dist/esm. Filing INF-342 to track.
eli: Short-term plan: 1) update quickstart README with cheatsheet + link to examples, 2) add example repos under examples/js/{cjs,esm,ts,edge}, 3) follow up with build normalization RFC.
nora: I'll add the onboarding checklist note referencing the new README snippets so support can point users immediately.
eli: Great. Thanks all — let's land the docs PR and ship the example apps before we change the build output. Closing thread.
